      "message": "I\u0027m sorry but could you elaborate details?\n\nI thought that both physical IOMMUs in VM DTBO\u0027s `/physical` and pvIOMMUs from crosvm DT have the same format (`id` only), and devices that uses IOMMUs has format `\u003ciommu_phandle (physical|pv)_sid\u003e, ...`. I thought this way because new VM DTBO format is just another way to represent `android,pvmfw,phys-*`, and we used to described phys IOMMU with `android,pvmfw,phys-iommu \u003d \u003cid1\u003e, \u003cid2\u003e ,,` and `android,pvmfw,phys-sid \u003d \u003csid1\u003e, \u003csid2\u003e ...`.\n\nAm I misunderstanding?",
