      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thank you for the correction. BTW, one follow-up question before uploading new patchset.\n\n\u003e  if \u003ctoken\u003e is now represented as a standard \u003creg\u003e, itself described by standard #{address,size}-cells, it can be parsed by libfdt from the VM DTBO transparently, for any size, and without needing extra code!\n\nI\u0027m sorry but I\u0027m bit confused here. Is `\u003ctoken\u003e` always `u64` (hence two cells) as you stated in your proposal and below? Or can it be changed to one cell if `#address-cells \u003d 1`?",
